  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "Saudi King Salman appoints Fayyadh Al Ruwaili, Chairman of the General Staff, as commander of the Saudi-led coalition in Yemen after government forces retreated near Bab al-Mandeb to Aden.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-16:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "On 15 November, PLC forces withdrew from the Bab al-Mandeb Strait and redeployed towards Aden.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386099969:387"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "On 3 September 2026, Iran-backed Houthis launched an offensive against the Saudi-backed Presidential Leadership Council (PLC), Yemen's internationally recognized government, amid the civil war.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386099969:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "On the map, you can see Bab al-Mandeb, the place the reports identify.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-16:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:33Z",
      "text": "On 11 November, Southern Resistance and the PLC cooperated to seize Jabal al-Nasirah and al-Mamdar from Houthi forces.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:week:1386099969:373"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:42Z",
      "text": "On 12 November, PLC forces claimed to have carried out 703 operations against Houthi-held positions.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:week:1386099969:375"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:51Z",
      "text": "On 13 November, the Houthis launched an offensive towards Jabal Kharaz, capturing al-Shatt and the Al-Sarih crossing, and on 14 November PLC forces claimed recapture of positions near that crossing.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:week:1386099969:376",
        "wiki:week:1386099969:377"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:01:02Z",
      "text": "The article lists two sides: Supreme Political Council and AQAP on one, Presidential Leadership Council and Southern Resistance on the other.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1386099969:side-1",
        "wiki:box:1386099969:side-2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:01:10Z",
      "text": "Wikipedia lists the conflict as ongoing.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1386099969:status"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:01:19Z",
      "text": "Aden is also named in the reports.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-16:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:01:28Z",
      "text": "The story is reported by Al Jazeera.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-16:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:01:36Z",
      "text": "Al Jazeera headlined it: “Saudi Arabia dismisses commander of coalition forces fighting Houthis”.",
      "cites": [
        "news:aljazeera:5de9237e8298"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:01:42Z",
      "text": "BBC News headlined it: “Yemeni forces retreat to defend port city from Houthis”.",
      "cites": [
        "news:bbc:e3c6bc678a27"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:01:48Z",
      "text": "France 24 headlined it: “Saudi Arabia dismisses commander of anti-Houthi coalition as rebels advance”.",
      "cites": [
        "news:france24:f6d733473972"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:01:57Z",
